  "short_description": "Non-canonical FirstPersonEmbodiment research layered on accepted CH9.6. S5 two-hand first/third-person presentation is accepted; S6 separates the 17-bone pose rig from concrete first-person hand geometry through a substitutable visual-provider boundary.",
  "purpose": "Evaluate first-person articulated one/two-hand held-item presentation, third-person held-item visibility and secondary-hand support, catalogued item silhouettes, grip profiles, substitutable hand visuals, clothing-visible viewmodels and low-latency item selection without reopening frozen CH9.6 and without weakening authority over concrete item actions.",
  "expected_outcome": "The selected canonical replica item resolves through presentation-only visual/grip catalogs. One-hand items occupy only the primary right hand. Two-hand profiles reserve the left articulated first-person hand and drive third-person secondary support. The first-person 17-bone skeleton and pose logic are independent from concrete hand geometry through a provider contract, allowing a later compatible authored/skinned visual implementation without changing grip, two-hand, Item Graph or network authority code. Empty/one-hand selection restores both left-hand presentations immediately. Concrete item mutations remain server-authoritative and hotbar selection remains transient/local.",
  "current_stage": "FPE-R2 S6 — substitutable first-person hand visual provider boundary",
  "stage_status": "RESEARCH_R2_S6_IMPLEMENTED_OPERATOR_RERUN_PENDING",
  "progress_note": "R2/S1-S4 remain accepted. S5 Fix2 corrected real replica definition precedence: canonical item/mount-base maps to beacon_mount_base, which must resolve mount_base before generic beacon tokens. The operator ran the full focused suite cleanly on 04976854: S2 catalog 27 assertions, S3 hand pose 20, S3 rig 23, S3 posed 17, S4 grip 20, S4 viewmodel 36, S5 secondary support 33, S5 third-person presenter 20, collision isolation 30, performance 10 and scene-load 22, ending with FirstPersonEmbodiment focused tests: PASS. Graphical evidence then showed slot 1 beacon as R:beacon_pinch with S4/S5 FREE, while slot 2 showed R:bulky_carry, L:support_cradle, S4 ACTIVE profile mount_base_two_hand and S5 ACTIVE FALLBACK_PROCEDURAL_ARM; the third-person fallback avatar visibly held the blue mount-base with both arms. S5 is therefore accepted for research progression. S6 adds FirstPersonHandVisualProvider plus SubstitutableFirstPersonHandRig. PosedCataloguedFirstPersonEmbodiment now consumes that rig. The default provider reproduces the existing 16 procedural palm/finger visuals, while a synthetic compatible provider gate proves that visual geometry can be substituted on the same 17-bone skeleton and pose transitions still work. Fix14 exposes provider mode in the graphical HUD. Accepted CH9.6 remains unchanged.",
  "last_accepted_checkpoint": "FPE-R2 S5 RESEARCH ACCEPTED: clean full focused suite on 04976854fa79c5be7150e766973567f53c66e8c0 plus graphical evidence of correct beacon one-hand and replica beacon_mount_base two-hand first/third-person support; accepted CH9.6 base e547ba52a440e72cc02c6bbe449edaf160bae7ab remains frozen",
  "next_stage": "Operator updates the detached FPE worktree and reruns RUN_FPE_RESEARCH_TESTS.ps1. New mandatory gate: FPE R2 S6 hand visual provider boundary: PASS. Existing S2-S5, collision, performance and scene-load gates must remain clean. Then run PLAY_FPE_RESEARCH.ps1. HUD must report S6 hand visuals L:PROCEDURAL_SEGMENTS and R:PROCEDURAL_SEGMENTS with substitutable:YES. Switching 1 -> 2 -> empty while moving must retain beacon pinch, mount-base two-hand first-person support, S5 third-person secondary support, empty-slot release, zero blocking hotbar path and no owner self-push. Production-quality skinned geometry is a later provider implementation, not part of the S6 gate.",
